\f4\fs26 Unloading \'93The Johnny\'94, as Cracker had decided to call him, was nowhere near as difficult as predicted and they managed to lug him to Cracker\'92s apartment before he became fully aware. Cracker wanted to dump The Johnny, shit be his name, on what masqueraded as a couch. Sarah insisted he required a proper bed, but had to settle for Cracker\'92s lumpy array of metal springs and exposed stuffing that waited in the bedroom.\
\'93Metal springs? Haven\'92t you heard of hydro-gel?\'94 The Johnny was now awake.\
\'93I suppose you want clean sheets as well?\'94 Cracker thought sarcasm was widely known, but The Johnny lumbered out of the bed and onto the floor.\
\'93Dirty sheets? Where am I?\'94 The Johnny looked around and was filled with disgust. \'93This place is deplorable.\'94\
\'93The decorator is coming next week.\'94 Cracker was not warming to The Johnny at all.\
\'93Have you got any?\'94 Sarah inquired, but was met with a blank stare. \'93Clean Sheets?\'94\
\'93Yes, yes.\'94 Cracker stomped out of the room and returned with a set of sheets, still in its original plastic wrapping. He\'92d pinched them a few months back and had them ear-marked for Christmas presents. \'93Clean enough?\'94\
Sarah and Cracker set to changing the sheets and to her immense surprise he seemed to know what he was doing, even though the task was made more difficult by the absence of a fitted sheet, he efficiently and skilfully scooted around the bed, each corner hospital standard. She stood back grinning and, as she watched, she became impressed, more than impressed, she felt herself admiring his domestic flair. 
\f5\i It was very peculiar, she thought, to admire someone for their ability to make a bed. I\'92ve heard admiration is usually gained for one\'92s ability to mess up a bed. Oh, naughty thought. 
\f4\i0 She giggled out loud before slapping a hand up to her lips.\
They gave The Johnny the aggregate of pain-killers Cracker had lying around and, when ferreted out of sock drawers, plastic tubs hidden in his rickety kitchen cupboard and from under the sink, he had quite a little pharmacy. The Johnny was quickly zonked out on the cocktail of pills and his complaints settled to a soft murmur before he finally slept quietly.\
Reflecting on their second outing, Cracker plonked himself in his couch and said, \'93A very strange day. I\'92ve forgotten why we went out in the first place.\'94\
\'93The disc!\'94 Sarah exclaimed, grabbing her breasts as she ran to the bathroom. \'93I completely forgot!\'94 A lapse of memory was completely unknown to Sarah and the feeling was very deflating. Locking the door behind her she thrust her hand inside her bra. Nothing. She opened her shirt and pulled her bra aside and was shocked to see what appeared to be a superfluous nipple on her right breast. She leaned closer to the aged mirror, found a spot that was clear of gunk and was horrified to see that her skin had begun growing over the disc and the bio-components were taking root. \'93Cracker, wake Johnny up. I have a bit of a problem here.\'94\
\'93He\'92s fast asleep, I can\'92t get a thing out of him.\'94 Cracker said through the door a couple of minutes later. \'93What\'92s up?\'94 \
The door unlocked and creaked open. Sarah motioned him in and was pale, sickly and frightened. \'93The disc is under my skin and I can feel it spreading out.\'94\
\'93That cannot be good. Give me a look.\'94 Cracker said innocently.\
\'93I have no choice, but can you promise you will act like an adult?\'94\
\'93Me? Absolutely.\'94 \
Sarah opened her shirt and exposed her right breast. \'93It\'92s under the skin!\'94\
Cracker looked closely upon the breast and even with an extra nipple it was truly magnificent to behold. He desperately wanted to grab that tit and give it a good squeeze. 
\f5\i I really knead to. Ha, Ha. 
\f4\i0 \'93I guess a doctor is out of the question?\'94 \
\'93The disc would be too hard to explain.\'94 She shook her head in resignation.\
\'93Well whatever we do, we should do it fast.\'94 Cracker hoped she had a plan, because in the presence of a bare breast, his brain refused to work.\
\'93If we cut the skin, one side of the disc to the other, around the edge, we might be able to pull it out with tweezers.\'94 Sarah said, detesting the idea.\
\'93I have razor blades somewhere here\'94, he pointed around the room, but could not break eye-contact with nipple. \
\'93Would you mind getting it?\'94 Grabbing either side of his face forcing him to look in her eyes. \
He took to the vanity cabinet like an alcoholic looking for that last hidden bottle, tearing out the contents of the cupboard and dumping drawers onto the floor before he located a packet of ancient double edged wafer thin blades. He quickly handed them to Sarah and returned to the important business of staring at an exposed breast. \
\'93I will hold it still and you make a half-moon cut, right around the edge and I will see if I can squeeze it free.\'94 Sarah grabbed her breast on either side of the disc and squeezed lightly. The disc popped up, pressed tight against the underside of the freshly grown skin. \'93Cut lightly, but with confidence.\'94\
He was shaking but managed to make a single clean curved cut one third around the circumference. Sarah squeezed and massaged the flesh, as if popping a giant zit, but the disc wouldn\'92t budge. Cracker, maddened by the proximity of a bare breast, could take it no longer, without warning and purely on cave-man instinct, he began sucking on that tit like an alcoholic after he had found that last hidden bottle. It was unclear whether it was the vacuum of his mouth or Sarah\'92s disgust that dislodged the disc, but it began moving.\
\'93Keep going, its coming. Got it, thank goodness.\'94 Sarah was breathing heavily and was most relieved. \
\'93What\'92s going on Sarah?\'94 The Johnny was at the door and Cracker was stuck fast, incrementally removing the disc with his mouth.\
\'93This is definitely not what it seems.\'94 Sarah was mortified, but remained still until the disc-ectomy was complete. \
Cracker turned around with the disc between his teeth, minuscule unseen drops of Sarah\'92s blood clinging to the shiny metal and his lips. His spat the offending alloy into the tiny grubby sink and carefully washed it clean, noting the disc seemed to be largely undamaged, but there were tiny tendrils half the width of a hair waving about like thirsty little leeches searching for a blood vessel. Incrementally they grew shorter before withdrawing completely into the metal, leaving a flawless gleaming surface. \
It took some pretty tricky explaining to satisfy The Johnny what he saw in the bathroom was a medical emergency, but Sarah managed to talk him around. \
\'93Yeah, I sucked it.\'94 Cracker raised his right hand for a high five, but there were no takers. \'93C\'92mon, you guys, don\'92t leave me hanging.\'94 He laughed boisterously, but was rightly ignored. \
Slightly groggy, the Johnny shook his head in disgust and returned to examining the disc with a magnifying glass and appeared intrigued by his observations. \'93How very interesting. Some of the bio-components seem to be missing, but if I am not mistaken, they are regenerating, Sarah.\'94\
\'93I guess the missing bits are still swimming around inside me. What does that mean?\'94 Sarah was troubled greatly and not feeling all that well, either. She had never been sick in her entire life and did not like the sensation of her body betraying her. 
\f5\i Is this what it is like for normal people?
\f4\i0 \
\'93I cannot even hazard a guess
\f6\b . 
\f4\b0 The existence of these discs was only a rumour and as far as I know, self-repairing circuitry is science fiction. A bio-quantum processor is decades ahead of our current technology, so no-one will know what will happen to you Sarah. We are in unknown territory.\'94 The Johnny was matter-of-fact about Sarah\'92s prospects. His head hurt too much to offer sympathy to another. \'93You will have to see a very discreet doctor and hope he doesn\'92t find anything wrong.\'94 \
\'93No. Doctors have to report abnormal results. I will have to wait and hope for the best.\'94 Sarah trusted her immune system would take care of any problems, but crossed her fingers for good measure. \
\'93It\'92s just a bit of goop. She\'92ll be right.\'94 Cracker\'92s ignorance was vast and covered most topics.\
\'93No, the goop, as you call it, is a biological emollient that is saturated with synthetic DNA. The program is embedded in the DNA and that DNA is in Sarah\'92s blood stream. There is no telling what will happen.\'94\
\'93We will all have to stay here for the night and see what it does to me. I am too tired and sore to make the trip to the management district and we must discuss all of this further.\'94 She was resigned to a night in the slums.\
\'93There is no way I am staying in this cesspool, I\'92m going home. I need a bath and a glass of Merlot.\'94 The Johnny didn\'92t find the idea any more palatable than Sarah.\
\'93No, you have concussion. You must stay here as well. Cracker make sure he stays here.\'94\
\'93The Johnny stays.\'94\
\'93Cracker you may use violence\'94 Sarah smiled.\
\'93I am going to, even if he behaves.\'94 Cracker\'92s reply made Sarah smile even wider.\
\'93Good night, Johnny\'94 Sarah pushed The Johnny in the direction of the one bedroom and crashed on the couch. Cracker took the bathroom and slept in the bath, a fate to which he had some considerable experience. He had long since taken to the practice of sleeping in the bath whenever he was enduring a bout of gastro-intestinal trouble. It was closer to the bowl and if he couldn\'92t safely traverse that small distance, he would just shit the bed. To some, a bathroom with a space wasting tub was an extravagance, but to Cracker it was a second bedroom with en-suite.
